  "oneLiner": "Model who may run a store, which baskets may be purchased, and how checkout responds when an external step fails.",
  "summary": "A university team built this Java/Spring marketplace around store ownership, delegated permissions, shopping carts, composite discounts and purchase policies. The distinctive engineering work is in the rules between those features: consent-based nominations, cascading revocation, stock reservation and compensating external actions. The archived source includes a Vaadin interface and substantial tests, while its current runtime repositories and several integration boundaries remain academic rather than production-ready.",
