  "decisions": [
    {
      "title": "Represent delegated authority as a graph",
      "implementation": "Store records nominationGraph and reverseNominationMap alongside per-store subscriber states and manager permissions. waiveOwnership performs a breadth-first traversal and removes all collected appointments.",
      "whyItMatters": "Revocation has consequences beyond the selected person. Explicit relationships make that cascade visible and give the team a common domain rule. This benefit is inferred from the code, not an author quotation.",
      "tradeoff": "The graph, role map, permission map and user-facing store-role map must remain consistent. The audit found stale graph-link and declined-nomination bookkeeping edges; this is a modeling decision, not proof of complete authorization correctness.",
