    {
      "title": "Build policy expressions from reusable components",
      "implementation": "Condition and Discount interfaces have simple and composite implementations. Store composition methods replace two top-level components with a composite; recursive DTO conversion feeds nested UI boxes.",
      "whyItMatters": "Product-specific requirements can be expressed using the same evaluation machinery instead of one bespoke checkout branch per promotion. The structure also gives the UI something concrete to explain.",
      "tradeoff": "Expression semantics, labels and numeric edge cases must agree. Exact-value and conditional-policy wording gaps are documented; no claim of a complete production promotion engine.",
